Added static typing to the edit_globals file using static constants from
the GlobalSettings class.  I ran into an issue where I was trying to add
global settings via a module but I couldn't figure out what to pass in
for the globals data type parameter.  Moving these to class constants
makes it much easier to know what setting to use for the global data
type and will make it easier for module writers.


Here is a sample of how I am using this:
```php
  public function addGlobalTeleHealthSettings(GlobalsInitializedEvent $event)
    {
        global $GLOBALS;

        $service = $event->getGlobalsService();
        $section = xlt("TeleHealth");
        $service->createSection($section, 'Portal');

        $settings = [
            'telehealth_registration_uri' => [
                    'title' => 'Telehealth Registration URI'
                    ,'description' => 'Registration endpoint URI'
                    ,'type' => GlobalSetting::DATA_TYPE_TEXT
                    ,'default' => ''
            ]
            ,'telehealth_video_uri' => [
                'title' => 'Telehealth Video API URI'
                ,'description' => 'The URI for the video bridge api'
                ,'type' => GlobalSetting::DATA_TYPE_TEXT
                ,'default' => ''
            ]
            ,'telehealth_user_id' => [
                'title' => 'Telehealth Installation User ID'
                ,'description' => 'This is your unique video application api user id.  Contact support if you have not received it'
                ,'type' => GlobalSetting::DATA_TYPE_TEXT
                ,'default' => ''
            ]
            ,'telehealth_user_password' => [
                'title' => 'Telehealth Installation User Password (Encrypted)'
                ,'description' => 'This is your unique video application api password.  Contact support if you have not received it'
                ,'type' => GlobalSetting::DATA_TYPE_ENCRYPTED
                ,'default' => ''
            ]
        ];
        foreach ($settings as $key => $config) {
            $value = $GLOBALS[$key] ?? $config['default'];
            $service->appendToSection(
                $section,
                $key,
                new GlobalSetting(
                    xlt($config['title']),
                    $config['type'],
                    $value,
                    xlt($config['description']),
                    true
                )
            );
        }
    }
```
